cdecl on OS-9 -- what was changed================================cdecl 2.4, comp.sources.unix volume 14 issues 90 and 91 (1988).Originally written by Graham Ross; the posted release carries later workby others.  ORIG/ holds it as released.1.  cdgram.c and cdlex.c are yacc's and lex's output, generated on the    host.  cdecl.c INCLUDES them ("The output of this file is included    into the C file cdecl.c") rather than linking them separately, so    they have to exist before cdecl.c will compile.  They are committed    here so that a rebuild needs only cc.  ORIG/cdgram.y and ORIG/cdlex.l    are what they were generated from.2.  os9tmpfile.c supplies tmpfile(), which this C library has not got.    It makes a uniquely named file under /dd/tmp, opens it for update and    unlinks it on close.3.  cdlex.c declares free() as void, which is what the C library here    declares it as; lex's own output had it returning int.cdecl.c itself is unchanged.ORIG/testset is the release's test input.  ORIG/testset++ (the C++ half)is not here: RBF filenames do not take `+'.  The C++ front end,c++decl, is not built -- this is the C build.